                                                "sense_id": "6b855f24-3a47-3f51-bd10-636f38c49240",
                                                "text": "The United States Department of Agriculture states that grubs cost the livestock industry from $50,000,000 to $100,000,000 each year. The average devaluation on grubby cattle is from 25 cents to one dollar per cwt."
                                            }
